  "Question": "During the softball season, Judy had \\(35\\) hits. Among her hits were \\(1\\) home run, \\(1\\) triple, and \\(5\\) doubles. The rest of her hits were singles. What percent of her hits were singles?",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(28\\%\\)",
    "B": "\\(35\\%\\)",
    "C": "\\(70\\%\\)",
    "D": "\\(75\\%\\)",
    "E": "\\(80\\%\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "E",
  "Solution": "The hits that were not singles total \\(1+1+5=7\\). Therefore Judy had \\(35-7=28\\) singles.\n\nTo find their percentage, divide the number of singles by the total number of hits:\n\\[\n\\frac{28}{35}=\\frac45=0.8=80\\%.\n\\]\nThus \\(\\boxed{80\\%}\\) of her hits were singles, choice \\(\\boxed{\\text{E}}\\).",
